-- title:
--   Component-trivial Pl-point of Pic⁰ reduces with proj=0
-- statement:
--   The setting is the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring inside $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, together with a complete dictionary for its geometric special fibre. The hypotheses fall into the following groups; each group's content is described, several groups being summarised.
--
--   **Arithmetic base data.** A prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$; an intermediate field $K$ of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ over $L$ with $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension of scalars of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. A domain $A$ which is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Finally an element $j$ of $K$, nonzero, whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ is the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant.
--
--   **The model.** [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ obtained from the pushout presentation of the two-chart model by the two structure morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-algebras `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` $=$ `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` and `chartAlgInf A ↥K j`; it is assumed proper.
--
--   **The geometric special fibre.** An algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$, an $A$-algebra; two schemes $C_1, C_2$ with morphisms $c_1, c_2$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, each proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral; closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ over $k$ into the base change $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{modelTo}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ k)$ (each $i_\bullet$ given as a morphism commuting with the structure morphisms). The hypothesis `hcover` states that every point of that base change lies in the image of the underlying map of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred` states that the fibre product $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ is reduced; and `hn`, `hn0` provide a natural number $n$ with $\mathrm{Nat.card}$ of the underlying type of $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ equal to $n$ and $0 < n$.
--
--   **Sections.** A section $\varepsilon$ of `modelTo` over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to$ the model composing with `modelTo` to the identity), sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and `hε₁`: $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equals the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange k ε`.
--
--   **Relative Picard data over $A$ and over $k$.** A designation $D$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a zero section) for the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `modelTo`, with `hrep` a nonempty witness that $D$ represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles cut out by `algEquivZeroCut`, whose predicate on rigidified line bundles is `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`: thus a Poincaré rigidified bundle on $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{modelTo}, D.\mathtt{toBase})$ satisfying that predicate, a universal property classifying such bundles on arbitrary $A$-test schemes by morphisms to $D.\mathtt{toBase}$, and triviality along the zero section. Further: `hsm` and `hsep`, that $D.\mathtt{toBase}$ is smooth and separated; `hreps`, the corresponding representability statement for the base change $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k$ relative to the $k$-base-changed curve and section; `hPk`, an isomorphism between the Poincaré bundle of `hreps` and the line bundle obtained by the base-change construction `BaseChange.ofR` from the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection $\mathrm{pullback}(D.\mathtt{toBase}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ k) \to D.P$; and designations $D_1, D_2$ for $c_1, c_2$ with nonempty representability witnesses `hrep₁`, `hrep₂` for the corresponding `algEquivZeroCut` conditions relative to $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$.
--
--   **The second component morphism.** A morphism $\nu_2$ from $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k).\mathtt{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathtt{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, together with `hν₂`: for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $a$ in $\mathrm{SchemeHomOver}\ t\ (D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k).\mathtt{toBase}$, the line bundle of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` pulled back along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification, in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.rigidify` along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` and $\mathrm{pullback.snd}\ c_2\ t$, of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1 i₂.2 t` of the line bundle of `hreps.poincare.pullbackAlong a`. Thus $\nu_2$ computes restriction of line bundles to $C_2$, rigidified along $\varepsilon_2$.
--
--   **The generic fibre as a curve model, and Galois equivariance.** Compatible $A$- and $L$-algebra structures on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$), an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ onto $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{modelTo}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ with `heη` saying that $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is $M_\eta.\mathtt{toBase}$. The preimage under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) is assumed nonempty, and `hMηpin` states that for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` corresponding under $M_\eta.\mathtt{ffEquiv}$ to the germ at the generic point of the regular function on that preimage obtained from $a$ has Laurent expansion equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffMap`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) of $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ applied to the expansion of $a$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$. The hypothesis `hgal` states that for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and every pair $x, x'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $M_\eta.C$ (sections of $M_\eta.\mathtt{toBase}$), if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\ x'$ equals the action of [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) on $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\ x$, where $\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ is the bijection between $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points and places.
--
--   **The special-fibre group dictionary.** A datum $G$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}$ of $G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$. Bijections $\mathrm{pts}$, $\mathrm{ptsI}$, $\mathrm{ptsE}$ from $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ onto the $k$-points of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ k).\mathtt{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathtt{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathtt{toBase}$ respectively. The hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` say that each bijection is additive up to isomorphism of line bundles: the Poincaré pullback along the image of $a+b$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the images of $a$ and of $b$, for the respective Poincaré bundles. The hypothesis `hproj` says that for every $x \in G.J0s$, $\mathrm{ptsI}$ of the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\ x$ equals $\mathrm{pts}\ x$ followed by the classifying morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and $\mathrm{ptsE}$ of the second component equals $\mathrm{pts}\ x$ followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   **Igusa identification of the components.** An integral weight-one form $w$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$, and curve models $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ and $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms ($e_\bullet$ followed by $c_\bullet$ equals $\mathrm{Mdl}_\bullet.\mathtt{toBase}$).
--
--   **The $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-level Abel–Jacobi data.** A bijection $\mathrm{gpts}$ from [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`, onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathtt{toBase}$, additive for the relative group law attached to `hrep.some` through `algEquivZeroGroupCut` (`hgadd`). Further: `hDL`, representability of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ condition by $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ L$ over the $L$-base change of the curve and section; a morphism $\mathrm{ajL}$ from the $L$-base-changed curve to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ L).\mathtt{toBase}$ over the base; a comparison morphism $k_L$ from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change to the $L$-base change of the model, with `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` expressing compatibility with the two projections (the second up to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$); a morphism $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$ and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\overline{\varepsilon}$ of $M_\eta.C$; `hPL`, an isomorphism of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the `BaseChange.ofR` base change to $L$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some` along the first projection; `hajLε`, that the base-changed section followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is the zero section of $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ L$; `hajL`, that for every field $K'$, every morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every point $x$ of the $L$-base-changed curve over $t$, the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` pulled back along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint` attached to $x$ with the ideal module of the one attached to $t$ followed by the base-changed section — so $\mathrm{ajL}$ realises $x \mapsto (x) - (\varepsilon)$; `hajbar`, that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ is $e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, $\mathrm{ajL}$ and the first projection of $\mathrm{pullback}(D.\mathtt{toBase}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ L)$, and `hajbar_over`, that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ followed by $D.\mathtt{toBase}$ equals $M_\eta.\mathtt{toBase}$ followed by $\mathrm{specMap}\ A\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hεbar` and `hεbar_aj`, that $\overline{\varepsilon}$ maps to $\varepsilon$ on the model and to the zero section of $D$ under $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$; and `hpts_aj`, that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $\mathrm{single}(\text{place of }x, 1) - \mathrm{single}(\text{place of }s, 1)$ whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic0.mk}\ Dv) = x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   **The place $Pl$ and the point $z$.** A valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits (`hPl`), a ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to Pl$ whose composite with the inclusion $Pl \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$; a comparison morphism $j_k$ from $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{modelTo}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ k)$ to $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{modelTo}, \operatorname{Spec}(\rho))$ compatible with the first projections (`hjk₁`) and with the second projections up to $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ (`hjk₂`). Finally a point $z$ of $D.\mathtt{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho)$, that is a $Pl$-point of $D.P$ lying over $\operatorname{Spec} Pl \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, such that the pullback along $i_1$ followed by $j_k$ of the line bundle of `hrep.some.poincare.pullbackAlong z` is isomorphic to the unit module of $C_1$ (`hcomp₁`), and likewise for $i_2$ and $C_2$ (`hcomp₂`); that is, the line bundle attached to $z$ is trivial on each of the two components of the special fibre.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists $y \in G.J0s$ such that, first, the underlying morphism of $\mathrm{pts}\ y$ followed by the first projection $\mathrm{pullback}(D.\mathtt{toBase}, \mathrm{specMap}\ A\ k) \to D.P$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by the underlying morphism of $z$, and second, $G.\mathrm{proj}\ y = 0$.
--
--   This is the special-fibre half of the statement that a point of the Néron identity component whose associated line bundle is trivial on each irreducible component of the geometric special fibre lies in the kernel of the projection to the component groups of the two pieces, here in the toric case of $X_1(Mp)$ with $p \nmid M$, whose special fibre over $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_p]$ is a union of two Igusa curves. It is the point-theoretic form from which the divisor-theoretic version, phrased in terms of classes $(x)-(s)$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is deduced in the level-lowering argument at $p$.
